+## Per-request native MCP metadata
+
+Authenticated in-process agent turns (`/v1/runs`, `/v1/chat/completions`,
+`/v1/responses`, and native session chat, including SSE) accept an optional
+`metadata.mcp` JSON object. For example:
+
+```json
+{"input":"Check the task","metadata":{"mcp":{"example/run-context":{"runId":"caller-id"}}}}
+```
+
+The native MCP client passes this object through the official SDK
+`call_tool(..., meta=...)` parameter as `params._meta`, separate from tool
+arguments. Model arguments and dispatcher kwargs cannot set or override it.
+The receiving server must authorize any claimed context: a gateway API token
+does not validate a vendor-specific schema or grant server permissions.
+
+Authentication precedes body parsing. A configured API key is required to
+supply `metadata.mcp`, including on manually wired no-key test listeners.
+`metadata` and `metadata.mcp`, if present, must be objects. MCP metadata must
+be finite JSON and at most 16 KiB of UTF-8 JSON using Python `json.dumps` with
+`ensure_ascii=False` (default separators); invalid values return HTTP 400
+before agent/tool execution. Other metadata keys are not forwarded.
+
+Snapshots are request-local, copied across executor/native MCP loop boundaries
+and reset on failure. They are not injected into prompts, history, response
+snapshots, session state or environment. Send them again on every turn:
+continuing a session or `previous_response_id` does not restore them. Missing
+metadata omits `_meta`; an explicit empty object sends `{}`. Idempotency replay
+can return an existing run without executing tools again.
+
+This transport ends at the in-process native MCP client. It does not forward
+metadata to a separate Desktop/live Bot Chat owner, a subprocess inference
+worker or an external relay. In particular, an already live canonical Bot Chat
+retains its existing owner handoff behavior, which carries only the message and
+author, **not** this transient context. Do not target that handoff for a
+metadata-dependent operation. No MCP plugin/bridge or vendor-specific runtime
+configuration is installed by this feature.
+
